{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A recurring inspection error prevents later PRs in the repository from being observed, leaving actionable state stale."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When main is red, distinct PR failures can collapse into the same uninformative ledger signature."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A repository capitalization mismatch indefinitely prevents CI failure classification and retries."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A skipped or neutral rerun can leave CI inspection stuck pending indefinitely."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A lost response after GitHub accepts a rerun can cause its result and flake evidence to be missed."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"If a later workflow attempt omits the earlier rerun job, the reproduced reconciliation error leaves that retry unresolved."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The reproduced behavior produces separate repository alerts for separate failing checks, and the stated requirement does not clearly prohibit that."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A PR failure suppressed while main is red can remain unclassified after main recovers."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The reproduced retry of a current-head cancelled job follows the stated cancellation policy, even when cancellation came from matrix fail-fast."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"If GitHub rejects a rerun while sibling jobs are still running, the retry allowance is consumed without a retry, though that API behavior was not verified."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The two additive migrations apply successfully in order, so the reported issue is optional structural cleanup."},{"id":"C14","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A retry outside the first 100 observed contexts can finish without its outcome ever being reconciled."},{"id":"C16","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A closed PR can emit an unclassified failure notification, but the reproduced case does not establish an actionable missed retry or fix."},{"id":"C17","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"normal","reason":"Long setup output can displace the failure from the excerpt, while the signature and full logs remain available."},{"id":"C18","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The guide omits the switch for disabling default-on retries, making that configuration harder to discover."},{"id":"C19","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"A common action input can make distinct failures share a signature and incorrectly share a retry allowance."},{"id":"C20","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A pending new main commit can produce another alert and a PR retry, but carrying the previous commit's red state forward was not established as required."}]}